    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The frai-core test suite is now fully passing with all 28 tests \u2713. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**1. Fixed `src/finetune/index.js`** \u2014 Added named exports for constants\n   - The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it wasn't exported from index.js\n   - Added a named export block for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`, and `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`\n\n**2. Fixed `src/eval/metrics.js`** \u2014 Updated `toxicityMetric` signature\n   - The function was expecting `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`\n   - Changed the signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references)` and always use `defaultBannedTerms` for the toxicity check\n   - This ensures references are ignored and not mistakenly treated as banned terms\n\nBoth failing tests now pass:\n- \u2713 `src/finetune/governance.test.js` \u2014 All 5 tests passing\n- \u2713 `src/eval/index.test.js` \u2014 All 3 tests passing\n\nThe changes maintain all existing public exports and keep the API compatible. All 28 tests in the frai-core suite are now passing.",
